# Safe wrapper to test a freshly BUILT hybrid, avoiding cross-build shader cache poisoning.
# Place beside eglantine.exe in the extracted GitHub Actions artifact.
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
$exe = Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'eglantine.exe'
if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $exe)) {
    Write-Host 'eglantine.exe not found alongside this script.' -ForegroundColor Red
    Write-Host 'Extract the GitHub Actions hybrid artifact and copy both Safe-Test-Hybrid files beside eglantine.exe.'
    Read-Host 'Press Enter to exit'
    exit 1
}
if (Get-Process -Name eglantine -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) {
    Write-Host 'Close other Eglantine windows first. Only one emulator can use this cache safely.' -ForegroundColor Yellow
    Read-Host 'Press Enter to exit'
    exit 1
}
$shaderRoot = Join-Path $env:APPDATA 'eden\cache\shader'
$titleId = '0400486024dec000'
$original = Join-Path $shaderRoot $titleId
$timestamp = Get-Date -Format 'yyyyMMdd-HHmmss-fff'
$backup = Join-Path $shaderRoot ("${titleId}_preserved_$timestamp")
$hasBackup = $false
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $shaderRoot | Out-Null
if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $original) {
    Move-Item -LiteralPath $original -Destination $backup -ErrorAction Stop
    $hasBackup = $true
}
# These are controls for a controlled A/B, NOT a guarantee of better rendering.
$env:EDEN_NX2_SPLIT = '2'
$env:EDEN_NX2_FENCE_BATCH = '1'
$env:EDEN_NX2_TENSOR = '0'
Write-Host 'Experimental B570 source hybrid. Test past the intro; note FPS + black-screen result.'
Write-Host 'Original Zelda shaders are moved aside while the hybrid runs and restored afterward.'
try {
    $p = Start-Process -FilePath $exe -WorkingDirectory $PSScriptRoot -PassThru
    $p.WaitForExit()
} finally {
    # Never delete a shader cache: archive the experiment's new cache to a separate folder.
    if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $original) {
        $trialCache = Join-Path $shaderRoot ("${titleId}_hybrid_trial_$timestamp")
        Move-Item -LiteralPath $original -Destination $trialCache -ErrorAction Stop
        Write-Host "Trial cache saved separately: $trialCache"
    }
    if ($hasBackup -and (Test-Path -LiteralPath $backup)) {
        Move-Item -LiteralPath $backup -Destination $original -ErrorAction Stop
        Write-Host 'Original Zelda shader cache restored.'
    }
}
$log = Join-Path $env:APPDATA 'eden\log\eden_log.txt'
$reportDir = Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'Trial-Reports'
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $reportDir | Out-Null
if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $log) {
    $report = Join-Path $reportDir ("hybrid_$timestamp.txt")
    Get-Content -LiteralPath $log -Tail 600 | Set-Content -Encoding UTF8 -LiteralPath $report
    Write-Host "Log report: $report"
}
Read-Host 'Press Enter to exit'

B570 Eglantine source-hybrid experiment (November 6, 2026)
===========================================================
READ THIS: This ZIP does NOT contain a compiled emulator. It contains a genuine
source integration/build recipe, built around the EXACT code revision of the
fastest build you uploaded. The integration and resulting gameplay are NOT
verified. An upstream source merge may have conflicts or not compile.

SOURCE BASE
* Fast initial Eglantine: upstream Eglantine commit 70fa082312
  (release: branch-switchbrew-names-736c1d29).
* Boot fix: WaitIfEqual64 from commit e736dfde9e / PR #567.
* Rendering fixes: PR #614, 11 separate commits, in order.
* GPU: Intel Arc B570 + Intel Core i5-14400F, Vulkan.

WHAT THE WORKFLOW DOES
1. Checks out original source for the fast binary (NOT its executable files).
2. Cherry-picks the startup fix and the Ocarina black-scene shader/upscaler fixes.
3. Stops with a precise conflict message if code cannot be combined.
4. If patching works, tries a Windows MSVC compile using Eglantine's CI settings.
5. If compilation succeeds, produces B570-Eglantine-Hybrid-Windows-x64.zip in
   GitHub Actions artifacts. No game data, keys, firmware, or saves are included.

HOW TO RUN THE CLOUD BUILD (no Visual Studio installation required)
1. Create a NEW empty repository on github.com. It may be private, depending on
   your GitHub Actions entitlement. You do NOT need to upload your game or ZIPs.
2. Open the new repository, choose Add file > Create new file.
3. In the filename box, type .github/workflows/b570-hybrid.yml
4. Paste the entire contents of the matching file in this ZIP, then Commit.
5. Open the Actions tab, select 'B570 Hybrid - fast Eglantine plus OOT rendering fix',
   then Run workflow.
6. If it succeeds, download the 'B570-Eglantine-Hybrid-Windows-x64' artifact.
   It will be a ZIP. Extract into a separate folder.
7. Copy Safe-Test-Hybrid.cmd AND Safe-Test-Hybrid.ps1 from THIS package beside
   the compiled eglantine.exe. Double-click Safe-Test-Hybrid.cmd.
8. Let the game reach the end of the intro. Close emulator normally. The wrapper
   backs up/restores the title-specific cache, saves the trial's cache separately,
   and exports a tail of the log into Trial-Reports. Upload the report back here.

IF IT FAILS
* If 'Apply startup and rendering fixes' fails, send the step log. It identifies
  which specific cherry-pick conflicts with the older source baseline.
* If compilation fails, send the FIRST compiler error (not just the last line).
* This test is exploratory. The older code might lack support required by PR #614.
* Do not replace or delete the three original Eglantine folders.
* GitHub Actions may be subject to account quotas / compute billing.

VERIFICATION STATUS
* The source commits and PR numbers were checked on the official GitHub pages.
* This workflow file was syntax-inspected offline.
* The integration was NOT executed here: this environment cannot access GitHub
  with git or compile a native Windows Eglantine executable.
* There is NO claim that the hybrid maintains 60 FPS or solves all gameplay bugs.

